      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "All docs builds are failing due to use of a removed unstable feature:\n\n* https://docs.rs/crate/bevy/0.17.0\n* Sub-crates like https://docs.rs/crate/bevy_platform/0.17.0\n\nExample build log:\n\n```\n[INFO] [stderr] error[E0557]: feature has been removed\n[INFO] [stderr]  --> src/lib.rs:1:29\n[INFO] [stderr]   |\n[INFO] [stderr] 1 | #![cfg_attr(docsrs, feature(doc_auto_cfg))]\n[INFO] [stderr]   |                             ^^^^^^^^^^^^ feature has been removed\n[INFO] [stderr]   |\n[INFO] [stderr]   = note: removed in CURRENT_RUSTC_VERSION; see <https://github.com/rust-lang/rust/pull/138907> for more information\n[INFO] [stderr]   = note: merged into `doc_cfg`\n```\n\nAs the note hints, this can be fixed by using `feature(doc_cfg)` instead.\n\nI would also suggest adding a CI test for `cargo +nightly doc --cfg docsrs` (or [the entire docs.rs environment](https://github.com/rust-lang/docs.rs/blob/master/README.md#build-subcommand)) to validate whether the build will succeed before releases.",
